</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To address <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q2</span>, we conduct rigorous ablation studies isolating core components of MoT’s dual-tinker architecture, as shown in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.1 Overall Performance ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
We evaluate four critical variations by disabling Information Tinker (w/o. Fusion and w/o. MoC) and Regularization Tinker (w/o. <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{con}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{con}</annotation></semantics></math> and w/o. <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{load}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{load}</annotation></semantics></math>).
➀ <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Edge Semantic Fusion Ablation.</span>
To evaluate the contribution of edge-wise semantic fusion, we replace it with a naive message-passing.
This ablation causes significant performance degradation across all domains and tasks, which confirms that our dynamic edge feature integration is essential for addressing model degradation.
➁ <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mixture-of-Codebooks Ablation.</span>
We replace the MoC with a single shared codebook architecture, which causes performance collapse, confirming its critical role in preventing representation collapse.
The disentangled latent spaces by MoC preserve domain-specific semantics and capture transferable domain invariances, which are essential for cross-domain generalization.
➂ <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Contrastive Loss Ablation.</span>
We substitute the <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{con}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{con}</annotation></semantics></math> with standard VQ loss and commitment loss <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> for codebook updates, which results in catastrophic performance degradation.
By enforcing geometric separability among cross-domain representations, <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{con}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{con}</annotation></semantics></math> prevents representation collapse in codebook and embedding spaces.
➃ <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Load Balancing Ablation.</span>
We disable <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{load}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{load}</annotation></semantics></math> and use the traditional load loss <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, leading to severe routing imbalance.
This proves the constraint’s necessity for balanced resource allocation across domain-specific codebooks, mitigating expert specialization bias.</p>
</div>
