<tr id="A2.T6.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">following relationships.</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Knowledge Graph</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Feature edge. Relation between two entities: <span id="A2.T6.2.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">&lt;relation name&gt;</span>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">E-commerce</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Feature edge. These two items are frequently co-purchased or co-viewed.</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Molecular Network</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Feature edge. Chemical bond. <span id="A2.T6.2.1.8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">&lt;bond type&gt;</span> bond, bond stereo is</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T6.2.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">&lt;bond stereo&gt;</span>, <span id="A2.T6.2.1.9.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(is/is not)</span> conjugated.</td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Edge Description Limitations in Text-Attributed Graphs</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We systematically catalog the raw edge descriptions of all text-attributed graphs used in Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix B Detailed Implementation of Empirical Study ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
Our analysis reveals a pervasive limitation:
<span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The edge texts exhibit extreme homogeneity, either through identical descriptions or rigid templates.</span>
This uniformity severely constrains the informational value of edge features, as they fail to capture edge-specific semantic nuances.
When processed by conventional GFMs using standard GNN encoders, these redundant edge descriptions contribute to over-smoothing phenomenon, where node representations become indistinguishable due to excessive homogenization of neighborhood information.
This fundamental limitation motivates our proposed edge-wise semantic fusion strategy, which dynamically enriches edge representations by integrating contextual node information, breaking the representation collapse while preserving structural integrity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.4.1 Why Information Tinker Alleviates Semantic Entanglement? ‣ 4.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4 Mixture-of-Tinkers ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.4.1 Why Information Tinker Alleviates Semantic Entanglement? ‣ 4.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4 Mixture-of-Tinkers ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> establishes a formal connection between edge-wise semantic fusion and information flow enhancement, providing a theoretical foundation for our architecture design in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Information Tinker ‣ 4 Mixture-of-Tinkers ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>
Using the variational lower bound for mutual information <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Z;\mathcal{E})\geq\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{E},Z}\left[\log q(\mathcal{E}|Z)\right]+H(\mathcal{E})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Z;\mathcal{E})\geq\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{E},Z}\left[\log q(\mathcal{E}|Z)\right]+H(\mathcal{E}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathcal{E}|Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathcal{E}|Z)</annotation></semantics></math> is a decoder reconstructing edge information.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{model}}=\mathbb{E}[\log q(\mathcal{E}|Z)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{model}}=\mathbb{E}[\log q(\mathcal{E}|Z)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The mutual information gap is bounded by:</p>
<table id="A4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Z_{\text{MoT}};\mathcal{E})-I(Z_{\text{vanilla}};\mathcal{E})\geq L_{\text{MoT}}-L_{\text{vanilla}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>MoT</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>vanilla</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>MoT</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>vanilla</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Z_{\text{MoT}};\mathcal{E})-I(Z_{\text{vanilla}};\mathcal{E})\geq L_{\text{MoT}}-L_{\text{vanilla}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Expand <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{MoT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>MoT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{MoT}}</annotation></semantics></math> using the embedding increment <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta Z</annotation></semantics></math> from edge fusion:</p>
<table id="A4.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{MoT}}=\mathbb{E}\left[\log q\left(\mathcal{E}\big|Z_{\text{vanilla}}+\Delta Z\right)\right],\quad\Delta Z=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(u)|}\sum_{v\in\mathcal{N}(u)}\mathbf{W}_{2}\mathbf{e}_{uv}+\mathcal{O}\left(\|\mathbf{e}\|^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>MoT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>vanilla</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{MoT}}=\mathbb{E}\left[\log q\left(\mathcal{E}\big|Z_{\text{vanilla}}+\Delta Z\right)\right],\quad\Delta Z=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(u)|}\sum_{v\in\mathcal{N}(u)}\mathbf{W}_{2}\mathbf{e}_{uv}+\mathcal{O}\left(\|\mathbf{e}\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Taylor expansion reveals the information gain mechanism:</p>
<table id="A4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{MoT}}=L_{\text{vanilla}}+\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]+\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>MoT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>vanilla</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{MoT}}=L_{\text{vanilla}}+\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]+\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Replace the unsubstantiated inequality with a rigorous bound using the Lipschitz property of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]\geq\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta Z\right\|^{2}\right],\quad\left\|\Delta Z\right\|\geq\alpha\left\|\nabla_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\mathbf{h}_{u}\right\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]\geq\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta Z\right\|^{2}\right],\quad\left\|\Delta Z\right\|\geq\alpha\left\|\nabla_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\mathbf{h}_{u}\right\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">The causal structure of edge reconstruction ensures:</p>
<table id="A4.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\left[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\left[\frac{\partial\log q}{\partial\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\right]\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\left[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\left[\frac{\partial\log q}{\partial\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\right]\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">This term quantifies the direct contribution of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> to reconstruction loss.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">When edge features are independent of node embeddings, cross-terms vanish:</p>
<table id="A4.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\Delta Z]\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\Delta Z]\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Combining these effects yields the final bound:</p>
<table id="A4.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E21X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(Z_{\text{MoT}};\mathcal{E})-I(Z_{\text{vanilla}};\mathcal{E})\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>MoT</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>vanilla</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(Z_{\text{MoT}};\mathcal{E})-I(Z_{\text{vanilla}};\mathcal{E})\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]+\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{Z}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]+\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E21Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta Z^{\top}\nabla_{Z}^{2}\log q\cdot\Delta Z\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E21Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta Z\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\Delta Z\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E21Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\alpha^{2}}{4}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\nabla_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\mathbf{h}_{u}\right\|^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\alpha^{2}}{4}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\nabla_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\mathbf{h}_{u}\right\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This proof establishes a direct information pathway (<math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\mathbf{h}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{e}_{uv}}\mathbf{h}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>) that amplifies edge-aware signals, mathematically justifying why our edge-wise fusion outperforms traditional aggregation schemes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.4.1 Why Information Tinker Alleviates Semantic Entanglement? ‣ 4.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4 Mixture-of-Tinkers ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.4.1 Why Information Tinker Alleviates Semantic Entanglement? ‣ 4.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4 Mixture-of-Tinkers ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> quantifies the representational advantage of mixture-of-codebooks, explaining the multi-domain scalability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>
Each domain <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned a dedicated codebook <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For codebook <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and codeword <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{m,i}\in\mathcal{C}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{m,i}\in\mathcal{C}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of correct domain-specific mapping is:</p>
<table id="A4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\left(e_{m,i},\mathcal{C}_{m}\right)=\frac{1}{K}\cdot\frac{1}{M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\left(e_{m,i},\mathcal{C}_{m}\right)=\frac{1}{K}\cdot\frac{1}{M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Assuming domain independence, joint entropy across <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> codebooks:</p>
<table id="A4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(S_{1},\dots,S_{M})=-\log p\left(e_{m,i},\mathcal{C}_{m}\right)=\log(M\cdot K)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(S_{1},\dots,S_{M})=-\log p\left(e_{m,i},\mathcal{C}_{m}\right)=\log(M\cdot K).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Mutual information <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Z;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Z;S)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:</p>
<table id="A4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Z;S)\geq H(S)-H(S|Z)=\log(M\cdot K)-\epsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Z;S)\geq H(S)-H(S|Z)=\log(M\cdot K)-\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> under optimal routing.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This demonstrates how MoC overcomes the <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log K</annotation></semantics></math> bottleneck of standard gVQ-MAEs.
The <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\cdot K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\cdot K</annotation></semantics></math> scaling explains why adding codebooks improves cross-domain generalization without increasing <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 4.5. ‣ 4.4.2 How Contrastive Alignment Mitigates Representation Collapse? ‣ 4.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 4 Mixture-of-Tinkers ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This lemma connects the contrastive loss geometry with collapse prevention.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>
The triple-contrastive loss in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 4.2 Regularization Tinker ‣ 4 Mixture-of-Tinkers ‣ Two Sides of the Same Optimization Coin: Model Degradation and Representation Collapse in Graph Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) is:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{con}=-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\frac{\exp\left(S\left(\mathbf{h}_{i},z_{i}\right)/\tau\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\exp\left(S\left(\mathbf{h}_{i},z_{j}\right)/\tau\right)+\exp\left(S\left(\mathbf{h}_{i},\mathbf{h}_{j}\right)/\tau\right)+\exp\left(S\left(z_{i},z_{j}\right)/\tau\right)\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{con}=-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\frac{\exp\left(S\left(\mathbf{h}_{i},z_{i}\right)/\tau\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\exp\left(S\left(\mathbf{h}_{i},z_{j}\right)/\tau\right)+\exp\left(S\left(\mathbf{h}_{i},\mathbf{h}_{j}\right)/\tau\right)+\exp\left(S\left(z_{i},z_{j}\right)/\tau\right)\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, the dominant terms become:</p>
<table id="A4.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{con}\approx c_{1}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{h}_{i},\mathbf{h}_{j}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{h}_{i}-\mathbf{h}_{j}\right\|^{2}\right]+c_{2}\mathbb{E}_{z_{i},z_{j}}\left[\left\|z_{i}-z_{j}\right\|^{2}\right],\quad c_{1},c_{2}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{con}\approx c_{1}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{h}_{i},\mathbf{h}_{j}}\left[\left\|\mathbf{h}_{i}-\mathbf{h}_{j}\right\|^{2}\right]+c_{2}\mathbb{E}_{z_{i},z_{j}}\left[\left\|z_{i}-z_{j}\right\|^{2}\right],\quad c_{1},c_{2}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Under hyperspherical constraint (<math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{h}_{i}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{h}_{i}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|z_{i}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|z_{i}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A4.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|\mathbf{h}_{i}-\mathbf{h}_{j}\right\|^{2}=2-2\cos\theta_{ij},\quad\theta_{ij}=\arccos(\mathbf{h}_{i}\cdot\mathbf{h}_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>arccos</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mathbf{h}_{i}-\mathbf{h}_{j}\right\|^{2}=2-2\cos\theta_{ij},\quad\theta_{ij}=\arccos(\mathbf{h}_{i}\cdot\mathbf{h}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Thus minimizing <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{con}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{con}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to maximizing angular distance <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We employ angular geometry to decode the contrastive loss dynamics, revealing how gradient forces naturally induce hyperspherical uniformity.
This proves why our triple-contrastive design prevents the representation collapse common in gVQ-MAEs.</p>
</div>
